## 2. Sources of truth (read in this order)

Project information is layered (`Maestro/core/project-memory.md`). Consult
**in this order**:

1. **`CLAUDE.md`** (this file) — how to work, rules and guardrails. Changes rarely, with weight.
2. **`STATE.md`** — done / in progress / up next / pending items. **The project's shared
   memory.** Always read it at the start and **update it at the end** of every session that
   changes anything relevant.
3. **`product/`** — canonical artifacts per phase (discovery, requirements, architecture,
   experience and, above all, **`product/04-specification/`** — the **functional** source of
   truth, technology-agnostic). Full tree in `Maestro/core/artifact-protocol.md`.
4. **Code + tests** — the implementation of the specification.
5. **`CHANGELOG.md`** — history of *what changed and why*, per milestone.

> When `product/04-specification/` and observed behavior diverge, the specification **wins**
> — and the divergence is recorded in `STATE.md`.

## 3. How to work (always)

1. **Sync before starting** (always start from the team's most recent work —
   `Maestro/playbooks/developer-onboarding.md` §Session start-up protocol).
2. **Read `STATE.md`** to know where the project stands. After a context compaction, re-read it
   (§In progress) before any action: if the summary contradicts the file, the file wins.
3. Follow the current phase's workflow (`Maestro/workflows/`; phases in
   `Maestro/core/lifecycle.md`), reading only what `Maestro/workflows/README.md` §What each
   session reads dictates, and summon agents as `Maestro/core/orchestrator.md` §Invoking an
   agent dictates (the agent's entry in `Maestro/agents/NN-category/CONTRACTS.md`, never the
   whole spec in your context). Do not advance a phase without the corresponding gate
   (`Maestro/core/quality-gates.md`); every gate leaves its record in
   `product/99-records/gates/`.
4. **Verify** before calling a change done (§Definition of "done") — whoever verifies is never
   whoever produced it.
5. **Close the session** as `Maestro/START-HERE.md` §Close every session dictates — the full
   list lives there and applies to every session, not just the first; in short: `STATE.md`
   updated, framework lessons in `FRAMEWORK-IMPROVEMENTS.md`, `bash
   Maestro/_meta/verify-project.sh` green.
6. **Propose the commit** (and the push) with a clear message once the block is green and
   verified — never do it without the user asking or confirming; on a dedicated branch, never
   directly on the integration branch (`Maestro/knowledge/permanent-rules.md` §Collaborative Git
   discipline). Tell the team what is left to integrate.

